/* ARDUINO IDE
Description
Most basic part of building a drone is to learn how to control the speed and direction of a motor. 
This is done by using a motor driver, in this case, the L293D. The L293D is a dual H-Bridge motor 
driver that allows you to control the speed and direction of two DC motors. In this example, I  
learned how to set speed and direction ofone motor.

Materials 
ELEGOO UNO R3, Power supply module, Fan blade and 3-6V motor, breadboard, 
9V battery, L293D, 8 jumper wires

WIRING
*Power supply goes on breadboard, ensure +/- line up with breadboard +/-
UNO GND -> Breadboard shared GND
UNO DIG 5 -> PIN 1 L293D
UNO DIG 4 -> PIN 2 L293D 
UNO DIG 3 -> PIN 7 L293D
L293D PIN 3 -> Red wire Motor
L293D PIN 4 -> Breadboard shared GND
L293D PIN 6 -> Black wire motor
L293D PIN 8 -> Breadboard (+)

*/

//CODE
int speedPin = 5;
int dir1 = 4;
int dir2 = 3;
int mSpeed = 255;


void setup() {
pinMode(speedPin, OUTPUT);
pinMode(dir1, OUTPUT);
pinMode(dir2, OUTPUT);
Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop() {
digitalWrite(dir1, LOW);
digitalWrite(dir2, HIGH);
analogWrite(speedPin, 255);

}
